            0.108
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "8.1.1 A simple pendulum"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.113,
            0.367,
            0.245
          ],
          "content": "A simple pendulum consists of a small metallic ball (called the **bob** of the pendulum) suspended from a rigid support by a long thread as shown in Fig. 8.7a."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.392,
            0.115,
            0.723,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "We did an activity in the chapter ‘Measurement of Length and Motion’ in the Grade 6 Science textbook Curiosity, where we observed the oscillatory motion of an eraser hung with a thread. Is the pendulum similar to that?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.73,
            0.109,
            0.893,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.27,
            0.34,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.436,
                0.221,
                0.454
              ],
              "content": "(a)"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.431,
            0.247,
            0.678,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.538,
                0.436,
                0.566,
                0.453
              ],
              "content": "(b)"
            },
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.321,
                0.461,
                0.546,
                0.479
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 8.7: A simple pendulum"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.484,
            0.745,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": "The pendulum at rest is in its **mean position**. When the bob of the pendulum is moved slightly to one side and released, it starts oscillatory motion. Its motion is **periodic** in nature because it repeats its path after a fixed interval of time."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.56,
            0.744,
            0.728
          ],
          "content": "The pendulum is said to have completed **one oscillation** when its bob, starting from its mean position O, moves to extreme position A, changes direction and moves to another extreme position B, changes direction and comes back to O (Fig. 8.7b). The pendulum also completes one oscillation when its bob moves from one extreme position A to another extreme position B and comes back to A. The time taken by the pendulum to complete one oscillation is called its **time period**. Let us now set up a pendulum and measure its time period."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.733,
            0.44,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": "**Activity 8.2: Let us experiment**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.77,
            0.743,
            0.809
          ],
          "content": " Collect a piece of string around 150 cm long, a heavy metal ball with hook/ a stone (bob), a stopwatch/ watch, and a ruler."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.813,
            0.505,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": " Tie the bob at one end of the string."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.837,
            0.743,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": " Fix the other end of the string to a rigid support such that the length of the string in between support and bob is around 100 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.898,
            0.743,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": " Wait for the bob to come to rest. Your pendulum is now ready."
        },
        {
